2026-11-24 19:02 Cause 1 (round precision -21, BSD): Lib js_math_pow calls the platform's C pow. BSD libm (msun & co.) returns pow(10, -21) one ulp high (0x1.2e3b40a0e9b50p-70, 1/x = 9.9999999999999987e20, printed 999999999999999900000); glibc and V8 return the correctly rounded 1e-21. Measured with node: V8's Math.pow(10, n) equals the exact path (10^|n| exact in a double, one IEEE division for n < 0) for every integer n in -22..22; the general rule (any integer base, exact power, reciprocal) does NOT match V8 (1294 of 1.2M negative-exponent cases differ), so the fix is limited to base 10, |n| <= 22 -- round's factor. Platform pow beyond that stays libm (k74).

2026-11-24 19:13 Cause 3 (10-leaks.t, Windows): not a leak. The subtest dies at its 7th case, the first that loads through the FileSystemLoader: the loader searched the tempdir by its absolute path, and 'C:/...' is no absolute path to node's POSIX path model (path.win32 comes later, documented in 0.001), so 'template not found' escaped render_string as a Lib::Error (the reports print Text::Nunjucks::Lib::Error=HASH). Reproduced on Linux with a 'C:/...' search path. Fix is test-side: the test chdirs into the fixture dir and searches '.', the loader scenario stays as it was. No lib change, no Changes entry.

